  'f.spend': 'Spending each month after retirement', 'f.spend.h': 'In today’s prices, raised with inflation for you',
  tip: 'Your retirement spending is typed in today’s prices, so the page raises it with inflation every year for you. Inflation starts at 3%, close to the world average: since 2000, consumer prices worldwide have risen about 3.5% a year on average (World Bank figures), and most countries sit a little below that. It swings a lot, though: world inflation jumped to about 8% in 2022, and US prices have risen about 3% a year over the past century. Set it higher if you want to be extra safe. If prices rise more slowly than you set, you’re left with money to spare rather than running short.',
