  'm.p11': 'At a glance, Your future has five levels. Not on track yet: the money runs out too soon, or leaves less than you want to leave, even with steady growth. Close, but fragile: it lasts with steady growth, but in fewer than 3 of every 4 possible futures for the markets. On track: it lasts in at least 3 of every 4. Rock solid: it lasts in 99 of every 100, even after a fall in the first year of retirement. Dynastic Generational Wealth: Rock solid, and with steady growth the pot never shrinks in any month of retirement, even at 5 times your spending. “A bad run of markets” is a bad case: worse than 9 in 10 of the possible futures.',
  'lv.f4.note': 'If you’re here, don’t worry about reaching the very top. Your money is already safe, and there are bigger things in the world for you to care about now than your finances.',
  'life.note': 'You’ve planned for your money to last to {L}, a very long life, and that pulls your level down. Planned to {a}, the same plan would be “{lvl}”.',
  'life.note.f': 'You’ve planned for your money to last forever, a very long life, and that pulls your level down. Planned to {a}, the same plan would be “{lvl}”.',
